    "summary": "I built a single closed hex cell: one full hex base, a solid cover on the bottom, a solid cover on top as the lid, and caps on all 6 sides. check_build found no rule issues and no mesh collisions. It measures about 220 × 218 mm across and 80 mm tall. That's bigger than the \"small\" you asked for, because one full hex is the smallest closed cell I made. The catalog does have half and quarter bases, but I didn't try them, so I can't say whether a smaller one closes up. I couldn't add a handle to the lid because none fit, and there was no matchbox prop to show inside. Whether it keeps the matches dry depends on the print material and how tight the seals are, which the configurator can't check."
  },
